{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>The bonds of death compassed me</b> — like birth pangs and ropes, and therefore it has three dots [on the letter bet], to distinguish between it and 'the bands of Manasseh' [in Judges, where the word is spelled differently]." "<b>And the streams</b> — He likened the enemy to water, like the king of Assyria to the river's waters; then 'the waters overwhelmed me.' Rabbi Judah HaLevi said: M\"K [thus?] for 'worthless men' is in the manner of prayer it should not ascend, and it is the enemy, and 'the bonds of' [in the next phrase] is a likeness to the bonds of death."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {1 "The abbreviation מ\"כ is unclear; possibly 'thus' (מן הכתוב) or a reference to a lexical form. 'Worthless men' renders בליעל. The syntax of Rabbi Judah HaLevi's remark is compressed and difficult; translated hyper-literally without smoothing."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:32.547366780Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}